<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of La Higueruela</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1431</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of La Higueruela was fought on 1 July 1431 outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> between the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-castile">John II of Castile</a>, led by Álvaro de Luna, and the forces of the Nasrid emir Muhammad IX. The Castilians won but did not attack the city; instead they backed a rival claimant, Yusuf IV, who briefly became emir as a Castilian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a>. The battle is depicted in a celebrated fresco at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-escorial">El Escorial</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-la-higueruela.jpg" alt="Battle of La Higueruela" width="320" height="231" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fabrizio Castello, Orazio Cambiaso, Lazzaro Tavarone · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Higueruela.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
